INT. BOWLING ALLEY PAWN SHOP - NIGHT

Behind the shoe counter, a cage of guitars and cameras. Lanes rumble beyond the wall.

VINNIE CASSANO, 50s, sweating through a bowling shirt. ODETTA BRIGHTWATER, 40s, in a trench coat, a revolver low at her hip. KEMAL DURAN, 30s, hands up, backed against the glass. TRISH MALONEY, 20s, behind the counter, phone in hand. LEVI SZABO, 60s, an old man in the shoe line, frozen with a pair of size nines.

ODETTA
Everybody stay calm.

VINNIE
I'm calm. I'm very calm.

KEMAL
(overlapping)
It's not what it looks like.

TRISH
Should I call somebody?

ODETTA
Put the phone down.

LEVI
(muttering)
I only wanted bowling.

Kemal drops a bag. Cash spills. Odetta nods at it.

ODETTA
(to Kemal)
You were going to run.

KEMAL
I was going to tell you.

VINNIE
Tell her what?

KEMAL
That it's his.

All eyes swing to Vinnie.

VINNIE
(to the room)
Don't look at me.

Odetta lowers the gun. A long breath. A pin falls somewhere down the lane.

ODETTA
Strike.
